<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE node PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD D-BUS Object Introspection 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd">
<!--
  PIN / signing-key credential lifecycle, exported on the SAME object path as
  Card1 (/org/librescrs/Agent/card/<n>). This interface is present on EVERY card
  object; a client discovers support by introspection, not by testing a
  capability bit. Each method returns the object path of a freshly-created
  Operation1 instance; the typed result rides the sibling
  org.librescrs.Agent.Operation.Credentials1 sub-interface exported on that same
  Operation path (Result signal fires BEFORE Operation1.Finished).

  This doc block is the authoritative wire vocabulary the platform mirrors
  (CDDL / KDE client / macOS) derive from: the closed verb enum, the full
  outcome-token vocabulary, and the credential-record key/value tokens all live
  here.

  === Capability gate (method entry) ===
  ManagePin, ActivateSigningKey and ListCredentials require the card to advertise
  the PinManagement capability (Card1.Capabilities bit 3, value 8). When it is
  absent the method throws org.librescrs.Agent.Error.UnsupportedOnThisCard at
  entry and NO Operation is created — the same precondition-gate shape as
  Card1.ReadIdentity (IdentityData) / ReadCertificates (PKI). A card that DOES
  advertise PinManagement but whose records expose no actionable credential is a
  VALID call: the Operation is created and its Result carries outcome=unsupported
  (ListCredentials instead returns an empty listing with outcome=ok).

  === Client authorization + rate limiting ===
  ManagePin and ActivateSigningKey route through the agent's client-authorization
  gate (polkit action org.librescrs.agent.credentials.manage, default-allow: the
  PIN(s) collected during the operation are the human-presence proof) and the
  shared per-caller rate limiter, both BEFORE any prompt. An over-cap caller is
  rejected at entry with org.librescrs.Agent.Error.RateLimited; an unauthorized
  caller with org.librescrs.Agent.Error.NotAuthorized. ListCredentials is a read
  (no card-state mutation) and is not rate-limited.

  === Outcome token vocabulary (result "outcome", string) ===
  Every completed management attempt reports exactly one camelCase token, carried
  in the Operation.Credentials1.Result payload:
    unspecified          no classified outcome (fail-closed / non-card failure)
    ok                   the operation completed on the card
    userCancelled        the user dismissed the prompt (no card interaction)
    missingFields        a required secret was not delivered by the prompter
    invalidPin           the presented PIN was wrong; retries_left is meaningful
    blocked              the credential is blocked; blocked=true
    pluginError          a card/plugin error reached (or may have reached) the card
    unsupported          the card/plugin does not implement this management action
    keyActivationFailed  the PIN verified but the on-card key ACTIVATE step failed
    cardRemoved          the card was removed before/while the operation ran
  The terminal Operation1.Finished(status, errorCode) carries the mapped
  (status, code) for the same outcome; the Result payload carries the richer
  detail (retries_left / blocked / pin_activated / key_activated).

  === Credential-record tokens (ListCredentials records) ===
  Each record in the ListCredentials listing is an a{sv} whose string-valued
  enumerations use these closed camelCase token sets:
    kind          "user" | "sign" | "puk" | "can" | "unknown"
    state         "unknown" | "transport" | "operational" | "needsChange" | "blocked"
    unblock_style "unknown" | "resetOnly" | "setsNewPin" | "unblockAndChange"
    recovery      "unknown" | "holderViaPuk" | "issuerProcess" | "none"
  See org.librescrs.Agent.Operation.Credentials1 for the full per-record key set.
-->
<node>
  <interface name="org.librescrs.Agent.Credentials1">

    <!--
      ManagePin: mutate one PIN credential addressed by pinId.

      pinId    REQUIRED, opaque, == a record id from the MOST RECENT
               ListCredentials result on this card (agent-synthesized, stable per
               card session). A client that never listed, or names an id absent
               from the latest listing, is rejected at entry with
               org.librescrs.Agent.Error.UnknownCredential — the agent never runs
               an implicit list inside a mutation (that could prompt for the CAN
               inside a call the user did not frame as a read).
      verb     REQUIRED, closed enum: one of
                 "change"        change the PIN (collects current + new in one modal)
                 "unblock"       unblock via the PUK
                 "activate_pin"  set the holder PIN from the issuance transport value
               Any other value is rejected at entry with
               org.librescrs.Agent.Error.InvalidRequest.
      options  a{sv}, all non-secret. Closed key set:
                 "activateKey"  b  — only meaningful with verb "activate_pin":
                                     continue into signing-key activation after the
                                     transport PIN is set. Paired with any other
                                     verb -> Error.InvalidRequest.
               Any key outside this set -> Error.InvalidRequest (undefined option).

      Method-entry errors (no Operation minted): UnsupportedOnThisCard (no bit 3),
      InvalidRequest (unknown verb / undefined option / illegal combination),
      UnknownCredential (unknown or unlisted pinId), NotAuthorized, RateLimited.
      All in-operation results ride Operation.Credentials1.Result +
      Operation1.Finished.
    -->
    <method name="ManagePin">
      <arg name="pinId"     type="s"     direction="in"/>
      <arg name="verb"      type="s"     direction="in"/>
      <arg name="options"   type="a{sv}" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="operation" type="o"     direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!--
      ActivateSigningKey: bring the card's signing key into service by verifying
      the operational SIGN PIN and performing the on-card key ACTIVATE in one
      locked session. Takes no arguments — the agent resolves the addressed
      signing-key credential from the most recent ListCredentials listing (the
      record advertising key activation). A card with the PinManagement bit whose
      listing exposes no activatable signing key is a VALID call whose Result
      carries outcome=unsupported (no prompt is raised). The collected SIGN PIN is
      the human-presence proof.

      Method-entry errors (no Operation minted): UnsupportedOnThisCard (no bit 3),
      NotAuthorized, RateLimited.
    -->
    <method name="ActivateSigningKey">
      <arg name="operation" type="o" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!--
      ListCredentials: enumerate the card's PIN credentials (status, bounds,
      capability flags). Requires the PinManagement bit. A pre-auth (CAN/PACE)
      card self-activates its channel during the read and may prompt for the CAN
      exactly like an identity read. The listing is the id namespace ManagePin /
      ActivateSigningKey address; the agent caches it per card session (dropped on
      any credential mutation that reaches the card, and on card removal). An
      empty listing (card advertises the capability but exposes no credential) is
      a valid outcome=ok result.

      Method-entry errors (no Operation minted): UnsupportedOnThisCard (no bit 3),
      Internal (credential operation dependencies not wired), RateLimited (the
      per-reader operation backlog is full; retry shortly).
    -->
    <method name="ListCredentials">
      <arg name="operation" type="o" direction="out"/>
    </method>
  </interface>
</node>
